# PROJECT: BUILD THE GUARD / EMPLOYEE APPLICATION

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a complete, secure, mobile-friendly Guard/Employee Application for my existing Security Services Management System.

The application will be used by security guards who work at different client sites. Guards must be able to log in, view their assigned shifts, verify their physical presence at the correct site, check in, check out, view their attendance history, request leave, and request shift swaps.

The application must connect to the existing React website, backend API, and database.

This is an employee-facing application, not an administrative dashboard.

The main objectives are:

1. Provide secure guard authentication.
2. Display each guard's assigned shifts.
3. Verify physical presence using GPS geofencing and a site QR code.
4. Record accurate check-in and checkout events.
5. Calculate attendance statuses automatically.
6. Provide attendance history.
7. Allow leave and shift swap requests.
8. Display notifications and important shift information.
9. Support mobile devices, especially Android phones.
10. Synchronize attendance with the supervisor and administrator dashboards.

Follow the existing project architecture and the requirements document.

Do not create an unrelated application or replace the existing website.

Do not build a separate native Android or iOS application. Build a mobile-friendly React Progressive Web App (PWA).

Do not implement payroll, invoicing, online payments, or recruitment as part of this application.

