## Login process

When a guard submits their credentials:

1. Validate the form.
2. Send the credentials to the backend over HTTPS.
3. Verify the credentials against the real employee account.
4. Check whether the account is active.
5. Confirm that the user has permission to access the guard application.
6. Apply authentication rate limits.
7. Apply the configured lockout policy.
8. Establish a secure authenticated session.
9. Redirect the guard to the dashboard.

The requirements document specifies a lockout after five failed login attempts.

Implement that policy using the backend rather than frontend-only counters.

Passwords and PINs must be securely hashed. Never store them in plaintext.

Use secure cookie settings if using sessions or cookies. If using tokens, follow the existing secure authentication architecture.

Do not store sensitive authentication tokens in insecure browser storage.

The guard must be able to log out securely.

When a session expires, redirect the guard to login and explain that authentication is required again.

