# 9. ATTENDANCE STATUS DISPLAY

Display the attendance statuses defined by the requirements document:

- Scheduled.
- Present.
- Late.
- Absent.
- On leave.
- Manual (pending review).
- Left early.

Use clear text and accessible visual indicators.

Do not rely only on color to communicate attendance status.

## Status rules

Scheduled:
The guard has an assigned shift but has not yet checked in.

Present:
The guard has completed an accepted check-in within the configured grace period.

Late:
The guard has completed an accepted check-in after the grace period.

Absent:
The guard has not completed an accepted check-in by the configured absence deadline, and no applicable exception exists.

On leave:
The guard has approved leave covering the relevant shift.

Manual (pending review):
An authorized supervisor has recorded attendance manually and the entry is awaiting review.

Left early:
The guard has checked out early according to the organization's attendance policy.

Default timing:

- Scheduled start: 08:00 AM.
- Grace period: 15 minutes.
- Absence deadline: 08:30 AM.

A valid check-in at 08:15 AM is still within the grace period.

A valid check-in after 08:15 AM is Late.

If no accepted check-in exists by 08:30 AM, the backend should mark the guard Absent unless an applicable exception exists.

These are configurable policies, not hardcoded frontend rules.

The backend determines official attendance status.

The frontend only displays the status returned by the backend.

